    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `GET /api/owners/{id}` to return `membershipTier: 'SILVER'` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise `'BRONZE'`.\n\nThis project generates its DTOs from OpenAPI and exposes other derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`) as `@Transient` getters on `Owner`, which MapStruct auto-maps into `OwnerDto`. I followed that exact pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipTier` readOnly string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `namesakeCount`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a derived `@Transient getMembershipTier()`:\n   ```java\n   boolean uniqueName = this.namesakeCount != null && this.namesakeCount == 0;\n   boolean hasEmail = this.email != null && !this.email.isBlank();\n   return (uniqueName && hasEmail) ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\";\n   ```\n\nMapStruct maps the getter into the DTO automatically, and the existing `RespondWithOwner` OfficeFloor function serves it unchanged. Both new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 0 failures/errors.",
